the darkest object in our night sky  is a black hole its gravitational pull  is so  immense that not even light can escape  it  as its mass increases it can trap more  and more  black holes can even swallow entire  stars  some astronomers describe them as the  darkest secrets of the universe  thanks to three scientists we all better  understand what they  are if there is a certain amount of of  of matter which is imploding  contracting then it's inevitable  that they will form what is a black hole  professor roger penrose from britain  reinhard genzel from germany and  american andrea guezz  are all credited with discovering  elements that make up black holes  and are the winners of this year's nobel  prize in physics  it was in 1965 that penrose first proved  what black holes are and how they form  describing them in detail and stating  that at their  center time and space ceased to exist  penrose went on to work with the late  stephen hawking who revolutionized our  understanding of time and space  professor pinrose from oxford university  was awarded half of the nobel prize  gonzalenges shared the other half for  discovering that an invisible and  extremely heavy object  governs the orbits of stars at the  center of our galaxy  together their work described  characteristics of black holes and super  black holes  most many times larger than the mass of  our sun  it wasn't until april last year that the  first image of a black hole was captured  blurry but visible this idea that  space which we we experience as humans  as separate from time  become commingled it's it's both  intriguing and fascinating and i have to  say these are the things that kept me up  at night when i was a kid  andrea guez achieved another milestone  by becoming only the fourth woman to win  a nobel physics prize  it's always been very important to  encourage  young women into the sciences  so to me it means an opportunity and a  responsibility  to encouraging the next generation of  scientists who are passionate about this  this kind of work into the field  following legends such as albert  einstein and stephen hawking  the winning trio of scientists keep  paving the way to better understand  former mysteries leah harding al jazeera
 

